WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:09.480
Every app, game and website runs on algorithms. Today you’ll learn to write instructions a computer can follow exactly.

2
00:00:09.480 --> 00:00:16.170
An algorithm is a precise, step-by-step set of instructions to solve a problem.

3
00:00:16.170 --> 00:00:20.650
Recipes, directions and dance routines are all algorithms.

4
00:00:20.650 --> 00:00:26.200
A computer does exactly what you say, in exactly the order you say it — never what you meant.

5
00:00:26.200 --> 00:00:27.850
Precision matters.

6
00:00:27.850 --> 00:00:31.520
Sequence means order.

7
00:00:31.520 --> 00:00:38.750
Swap two steps and you can get a completely different result.

8
00:00:38.750 --> 00:00:43.050
The same idea in Python’s turtle module looks like: forward(100), right(90), forward(50).

9
00:00:43.050 --> 00:00:47.000
Blocks and text code share the same thinking.

10
00:00:47.000 --> 00:00:50.140
Great work! Let’s remember what we learned.

11
00:00:50.140 --> 00:00:54.440
Now build along, then try the challenges. You’ve got this!
